I agree with the reviewer's points. The main fixes are: (1) P6 is not ready to reuse — T0 must add the missing failure exit and copy-before-audit behavior; (2) the animal-shape claim is overgeneralized — change it to 'worse than the original weights for this config'; (3) keep head/body separate for now unless a minimal case proves otherwise; (4) add a minimal motion gate between T2 and T3; (5) ban per-clip ad-hoc angles, not normal coordinate transforms; (6) define 105 px as character height per Style E; (7) add final acceptance counts for repair count and labor time; (8) license wording should be 'retain source and usage records, verify when introducing code/skills/assets'. Budget caps stay: 12 image generations and 150 credits as hard limits; get a T3 rigging quote first; run one candidate end-to-end before expanding to 4 candidates per part; T0 costs no credits and needs no Nov 4 wait.
